Messages database and typedstream (milestone 3)
-----------------------------------------------

The Messages-database code in crates/oma-messages, including its
typedstream (NSArchiver) decoder, is a clean-room implementation written
from the facts recorded in docs/supported-formats.md; the sources consulted
for each file are listed in scripts/fixtures/PROVENANCE.md. No code was
copied from any of the projects below, and none of them is distributed
with this product:

- imessage-exporter and imessage-database (GPL-3.0): column names, numeric
  codes and key names were taken as facts from its source and
  documentation, and its release binary was run as a black-box test
  oracle.
- pytypedstream (LGPL-3.0-or-later): run as a black-box test oracle
  against the synthetic typedstream vectors.
- C. Sardegna, "Inside imessage-exporter: Reverse Engineering Apple's
  typedstream Format" (2025): format facts.
- The libmagic "Apple/NeXT typedstream" entry (BSD-2-Clause): header facts.

Some facts about the Messages database were taken from ChatExportKnowledge
(https://github.com/ChatExport/ChatExportKnowledge), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). They are restated in our
own words in docs/supported-formats.md (source S8); no text was copied.

